    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0312" n="200" xml:id="pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4109: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1919-03-20T11:31:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1919-03-19T14:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 20, 1919, 11:31
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following repeated from [Harris at] Harbin.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d195-f1"/></p>
                <p>“192. March 19, 2 p.m. It is officially announced that the operations against Ufa
                    have been successful and the city was captured by Siberian Army March 13.
                    Junction point of Chishmy was also captured a little later. Harris.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d195-f1" n="4" xml:id="d195-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was sent by Consul General Harris while on his way east for
                    conferences at Vladivostok and Tokyo.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
